Chapter: ProbePreludeCollide
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Can a Codex program declare a name the zig prelude already declares?

 `zig-sanitize` renames a name that appears in `zig-prelude-decls` by
 appending an underscore, and that list is described in the emitter as "the
 UNION over the whole prelude". It is not. The prelude has 96 top-level
 declarations and the list names 23 of them: `std`, `main`, `cx_entry` and the
 file-scope `const`/`var` globals. The other 74 -- every `fn`, including
 `cx_print`, `cx_new`, `cx_concat`, `cx_text_eq` -- are absent.

 The reason is in the deriving script rather than in anybody's judgement.
 `build/check-zig-prelude-surface.ps1` reads emitted output for `const NAME`,
 `var NAME`, `|capture|` and function PARAMETERS, and never for the function's
 own name. It has been printing OK over a surface missing three quarters of
 the declarations.

 EVERY DEFINITION HERE IS CALLED TWICE AND NONE IS A LEAF. The first version
 of this probe defined `cx-print` and `cx-new`, called each once, and passed
 byte-identical on both arms -- because `inline-leaf-calls` and
 `inline-single-caller` had removed both before the emitter ever saw them.
 A probe that the optimiser deletes tests nothing. Two call sites defeats
 `inline-single-caller`; calling a helper defeats `inline-leaf-calls`.

 Bare metal does not care either way: prelude names are a zig concept and
 nothing on that arm collides. The zig arm is where the question lives.

Section: Main

  cx-bump : Integer -> Integer
  cx-bump (n) = n + 1

  cx-print : Integer -> Integer
  cx-print (n) = cx-bump n + 1

  cx-new : Integer -> Integer
  cx-new (n) = cx-bump n * 2

  cx-concat : Integer -> Integer
  cx-concat (n) = cx-bump n + cx-print n

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni ("cx-print 41  : " & show (cx-print 41))
   print-line-uni ("cx-print 10  : " & show (cx-print 10))
   print-line-uni ("cx-new 21    : " & show (cx-new 21))
   print-line-uni ("cx-new 5     : " & show (cx-new 5))
   print-line-uni ("cx-concat 7  : " & show (cx-concat 7))
   print-line-uni ("cx-concat 2  : " & show (cx-concat 2))
   print-line-uni ("cx-bump 99   : " & show (cx-bump 99))
  end
